  ('1132602361392888857', 'Passage of Venus', 1874, 'Documentary', 'P.J.C. Janssen, Francisco Antônio de Almeida Júnior', null, null, null, 'Photo sequence of the rare transit of Venus over the face of the Sun, one of the first chronophotographic sequences. In 1873, P.J.C. Janssen, or Pierre Jules César Janssen, invented the Photographic Revolver, which captured a series of images in a row. The device, automatic, produced images in a row without human intervention, being used to serve as photographic evidence of the passage of Venus before the Sun, in 1874.', 'Photo sequence of the rare transit of Venus over the face of the Sun, one of the first chronophotographic sequences. In 1873, P.J.C. Janssen, or Pierre Jules César Janssen, invented the Photographic Revolver, which captured a series of images in a row. The device, automatic, produced images in a row without human intervention, being used to serve as photographic evidence of the passage of Venus before the Sun, in 1874.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/XWPDZzK7N2WQcejI8W96IxZEeP.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:315946'),
  ('576284726358274678', 'Passage to Marseille', 1944, 'Adventure, War, Action', 'Michael Curtiz, James Wong Howe', 'Jack Moffitt, Casey Robinson', 'Humphrey Bogart, Claude Rains, Michèle Morgan, Philip Dorn, Sydney Greenstreet, Peter Lorre, George Tobias, Helmut Dantine', null, 'A freedom-loving French journalist sacrifices his happiness and security to battle Nazi tyranny.', 'A freedom-loving French journalist sacrifices his happiness and security to battle Nazi tyranny.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/14s5iMOLt8EboZmnltXjB7g2sap.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:18229'),
  ('1013019936888307079', 'Passages', 2023, 'Romance, Drama', 'Ira Sachs, Grégoire Jeudy, Julie-Anne Simon', 'Mauricio Zacharias, Ira Sachs', 'Franz Rogowski, Ben Whishaw, Adèle Exarchopoulos, Erwan Kepoa Falé, Théo Cholbi, Arcadi Radeff, Léa Boublil, Thibault Carterot', 'NR', 'Tomas and Martin are a gay couple living in Paris whose marriage is thrown into crisis when Tomas impulsively begins a passionate affair with young schoolteacher Agathe. But when Martin begins an affair of his own, Tomas must confront life decisions he may be unprepared—or unwilling—to deal with.', 'Tomas and Martin are a gay couple living in Paris whose marriage is thrown into crisis when Tomas impulsively begins a passionate affair with young schoolteacher Agathe. But when Martin begins an affair of his own, Tomas must confront life decisions he may be unprepared—or unwilling—to deal with.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/8GR7s4YiyFswOmTibfKCYAPxT9k.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:898673'),
  ('972003199282620285', 'Passagier 23', 2018, 'Thriller, TV Movie', 'Ian Blumers, Regina Ziegler, Alexander Dierbach', 'Miriam Rechel', 'Lucas Gregorowicz, Picco von Groote, Oliver Mommsen, Liane Forestieri, Judy Winter, Mercedes Müller, Aurel Manthei, André Röhner', null, 'It''s been five years Martin''s family vanished without a trace from a cruise ship. Ever since, the police psychologist is tortured by the thought of his wife having committed a murder-suicide, taking their son with her. He is the only one not willing to believe this. Suddenly, a new lead takes him back aboard the very same luxury cruiser, where once again, a mother and her child have vanished. But this time, the girl reappears - holding a teddy bear that used to belong to Martin''s son. Martin soon learns that things are handled differently on the open sea. Not to disturb his passengers'' enjoyment of the lavish luxuries of their cruise, the rich owner of the cruiser wants to keep the child out of sight and hides her deep under deck in the quarantine bay. Here, Martin tries to get the traumatized girl to talk to him. But even deeper in the dark underbelly of the ship there is something lurking. And all signs point to a serial killer, just waiting to strike again.', 'It''s been five years Martin''s family vanished without a trace from a cruise ship. Ever since, the police psychologist is tortured by the thought of his wife having committed a murder-suicide, taking their son with her. He is the only one not willing to believe this. Suddenly, a new lead takes him back aboard the very same luxury cruiser, where once again, a mother and her child have vanished. But this time, the girl reappears - holding a teddy bear that used to belong to Martin''s son. Martin soon learns that things are handled differently on the open sea. Not to disturb his passengers'' enjoyment of the lavish luxuries of their cruise, the rich owner of the cruiser wants to keep the child out of sight and hides her deep under deck in the quarantine bay. Here, Martin tries to get the traumatized girl to talk to him. But even deeper in the dark underbelly of the ship there is something lurking. And all signs point to a serial killer, just waiting to strike again.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/3HOzjKO3GrtO29LSWWRi5nJrLJw.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:567623'),
  ('391849018877620824', 'Passagrana', 2024, 'Comedy', 'Ravel Cabral, Carlos André Zalasik, Diana Galantini', 'Ravel Cabral', 'Wesley Guimarães, Juan Queiroz, Elzio Vieira, Wenry Bueno, Giovanna Grigio, Carol Castro, Luciana Paes, Marco Luque', null, 'Four friends are tired of surviving by pulling small scams and running from the police. After a swindle that goes wrong, the quartet formed by Zoinhu, Linguinha, Mãodelo and Alãodelom comes across a robbery that could take them off the streets.', 'Four friends are tired of surviving by pulling small scams and running from the police. After a swindle that goes wrong, the quartet formed by Zoinhu, Linguinha, Mãodelo and Alãodelom comes across a robbery that could take them off the streets.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/g9tAi6v6cinBDItrW0fW4HoweNq.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:1098088'),
  ('25656355521246240', 'Passchendaele', 2008, 'Drama, Romance, War, History', 'Paul Gross, Kimberley Zaharko, Gregory Middleton', 'Paul Gross', 'Paul Gross, Caroline Dhavernas, Joe Dinicol, Meredith Bailey, Adam J. Harrington, Gil Bellows, James Kot, Jesse Frechette', 'NR', 'Sergeant Michael Dunne fights in the 10th Battalion, AKA The "Fighting Tenth" with the 1st Canadian Division and participated in all major Canadian battles of the war, and set the record for highest number of individual bravery awards for a single battle', 'Sergeant Michael Dunne fights in the 10th Battalion, AKA The "Fighting Tenth" with the 1st Canadian Division and participated in all major Canadian battles of the war, and set the record for highest number of individual bravery awards for a single battle', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/2FMtSxzF2fR5dx5was9Kftjag0U.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:14582'),
  ('769967968980729088', 'Passed Away', 1992, 'Comedy', 'Charlie Peters, Arthur Albert', 'Charlie Peters', 'Bob Hoskins, Blair Brown, Tim Curry, Frances McDormand, William Petersen, Pamela Reed, Peter Riegert, Maureen Stapleton', 'PG-13', 'Thrown for a loop by the unexpected news that Dad has suddenly gone to his reward, the grieving eccentric Scanian clan are drawn together in a test of familial endurance that soon has them at each other''s throats.', 'Thrown for a loop by the unexpected news that Dad has suddenly gone to his reward, the grieving eccentric Scanian clan are drawn together in a test of familial endurance that soon has them at each other''s throats.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kUBxt3YGBOg5Okpg6dUE7DBrRgR.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:62383'),
  ('1133615123002904759', 'Passed by Censor', 2019, 'Drama', 'Serhat Karaaslan, Meryem Yavuz', 'Serhat Karaaslan', 'Berkay Ateş, Füsun Demirel, İpek Türktan, Saadet Işıl Aksoy, Erdem Şenocak, Müfit Kayacan, Banu Fotocan, S. Emrah Özdemir', null, 'In the heart of Istanbul''s prison, Zakir controls the letters prisoners receive. His average day is spent between the censorship office, his colleagues and his evening writing class. For a writing assignment, he steals a photo from one of the letters, in which appears Selma, an inmate''s wife. More than an inspiration, she becomes an obsession for Zakir. He observes her, makes up stories, and imagines the worst to the extent that he puts himself at great risk.', 'In the heart of Istanbul''s prison, Zakir controls the letters prisoners receive. His average day is spent between the censorship office, his colleagues and his evening writing class. For a writing assignment, he steals a photo from one of the letters, in which appears Selma, an inmate''s wife. More than an inspiration, she becomes an obsession for Zakir. He observes her, makes up stories, and imagines the worst to the extent that he puts himself at great risk.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/5hatJuGsPlWTlVdxafdvY7GSwjL.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:567940'),
