  ('601432402809443813', 'Pharmaceutical Hallucinations', 1908, 'Fantasy', 'Georges Méliès', null, 'Bleuette Bernon', null, 'There''s a chemistry lab, in which one or two people ingest the wrong drug -- apparently -- and have a seriously bad trip. Then there''s this wizard in his cave, and a fairy appears -- then there''s this massive feast with about a dozen people. Then it ends.', 'There''s a chemistry lab, in which one or two people ingest the wrong drug -- apparently -- and have a seriously bad trip. Then there''s this wizard in his cave, and a fairy appears -- then there''s this massive feast with about a dozen people. Then it ends.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/4ULy7s6wpr1VlKPnJPkmcNgI0fD.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:196662'),
  ('506139643654164614', 'Pharos of Chaos', 1983, 'Documentary', 'Manfred Blank, Wolf-Eckart Bühler, Bernd Fiedler', 'Hella Kothmann', 'Charles Brauer, Sterling Hayden, Burkhard Driest, Hannes Wader, Hanns Zischler', 'PG-13', 'A superb, moving and thrilling interview with American actor Sterling Hayden (1916-86), held in Besançon, France, on board a dilapidated barge, when he was 65 years old. An unparalleled portrait, in his own words and without any qualms, of a legendary Hollywood star, icon of film noir and the western, who was also a marine, an OSS agent, an anti-communist informer, a writer and a wandering sailor: the hero of his own life.', 'A superb, moving and thrilling interview with American actor Sterling Hayden (1916-86), held in Besançon, France, on board a dilapidated barge, when he was 65 years old. An unparalleled portrait, in his own words and without any qualms, of a legendary Hollywood star, icon of film noir and the western, who was also a marine, an OSS agent, an anti-communist informer, a writer and a wandering sailor: the hero of his own life.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/lNGdhcY10erBsIWn6LlD5rzSoa7.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:348224'),
