  ('206653605741681718', 'Postal', 2007, 'Comedy, Action, Adventure, Crime, Thriller', 'Uwe Boll, Mathias Neumann, Bryan C. Knight', 'Uwe Boll, Bryan C. Knight', 'Zack Ward, Dave Foley, Chris Coppola, Jackie Tohn, J.K. Simmons, Ralf Moeller, Verne Troyer, Chris Spencer', 'R', 'The story begins with a regular Joe who tries desperately to seek employment, but embarks on a violent rampage when he teams up with cult leader Uncle Dave. Their first act is to heist an amusement park, only to learn that the Taliban are planning the same heist as well. Chaos ensues, and now the Postal Dude must not only take on terrorists but also political figures.', 'The story begins with a regular Joe who tries desperately to seek employment, but embarks on a violent rampage when he teams up with cult leader Uncle Dave. Their first act is to heist an amusement park, only to learn that the Taliban are planning the same heist as well. Chaos ensues, and now the Postal Dude must not only take on terrorists but also political figures.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/gfU7ZYQEOVI06eZBjTAMnrzTLL.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:2728'),
  ('494664760503379341', 'Postcard', 2010, 'War, Drama, Romance', 'Kaneto Shindō', 'Kaneto Shindō', 'Etsushi Toyokawa, Naomasa Musaka, Shinobu Otake, Akira Emoto, Mitsuko Baisho, Masahiko Tsugawa, Ren Osugi, Yasuhito Ohchi', null, 'Toward the end of World War II, middle-aged soldier Keita is entrusted with a postcard from a comrade who is sure he will die in battle. After the war ends, Keita visits his comrade''s wife Yuko and bears witness to the tragic life she has led.', 'Toward the end of World War II, middle-aged soldier Keita is entrusted with a postcard from a comrade who is sure he will die in battle. After the war ends, Keita visits his comrade''s wife Yuko and bears witness to the tragic life she has led.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/pAJGv1Tg7sj8Kzsgvs3gueO8I1u.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:133160'),
  ('805188503645045058', 'Postcards from Leningrad', 2007, 'Drama', 'Mariana Rondón, Micaela Cajahuaringa', 'Mariana Rondón', 'Laureano Olivares, Greisy Mena, William Cifuentes, Haydee Faverola, María Fernanda Ferro, Ignacio Márquez, Oswaldo Hidalgo, Claudia Usubillaga', null, 'During the armed uprisings of the sixties in Venezuela, a young guerrilla woman has to give birth in secret. To her surprise, her daughter is the first to be born on Mother''s Day and photos appear in the press. Since then, both have to flee. Disguises, false names are the hiding places and the daily life of CHICA, the narrator of this story. Together with her cousin TEO, they reinvent the adventures of their guerrilla fathers, building a fantastic labyrinth of superheroes and strategies around armed subversion, where you never know where reality or madness begins. But the children''s game cannot hide the death, torture, accusations and betrayals that live inside the guerrilla.', 'During the armed uprisings of the sixties in Venezuela, a young guerrilla woman has to give birth in secret. To her surprise, her daughter is the first to be born on Mother''s Day and photos appear in the press. Since then, both have to flee. Disguises, false names are the hiding places and the daily life of CHICA, the narrator of this story. Together with her cousin TEO, they reinvent the adventures of their guerrilla fathers, building a fantastic labyrinth of superheroes and strategies around armed subversion, where you never know where reality or madness begins. But the children''s game cannot hide the death, torture, accusations and betrayals that live inside the guerrilla.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/A7N3DdYPwNXibztQC8CeM87i1sz.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:91825'),
  ('656514607908691646', 'Postcards from the Edge', 1990, 'Comedy, Drama', 'Mike Nichols, Michael Haley, Nathalie Vadim', 'Carrie Fisher', 'Meryl Streep, Shirley MacLaine, Dennis Quaid, Gene Hackman, Richard Dreyfuss, Rob Reiner, Mary Wickes, Conrad Bain', 'R', 'A substance-addicted actress tries to look on the bright side even as she''s forced to move back in with her mother to avoid unemployment.', 'A substance-addicted actress tries to look on the bright side even as she''s forced to move back in with her mother to avoid unemployment.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/uF7bO5UcenRgag0jpbVvKsGyfBK.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:22414'),
  ('943176426734441955', 'Poster Boy', 2004, 'Comedy, Drama, Romance', 'Zak Tucker, Wolfgang Held, Luke Geissbühler', 'Ryan Shiraki, Lecia Rosenthal', 'Jack Noseworthy, Matt Newton, Valerie Geffner, Austin Lysy, Lorri Bagley, Neal Huff, Ian Reed Kesler, Ebon Moss-Bachrach', 'R', 'The gay son of a conservative senator who is also the poster boy for his father''s re-election unknowingly befriends a gay activist bent on destroying the hypocritical campaign.', 'The gay son of a conservative senator who is also the poster boy for his father''s re-election unknowingly befriends a gay activist bent on destroying the hypocritical campaign.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/bDx4n2ZrQeeJJyJ2k6O2PVP4oO6.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:17651'),
